## CRITICAL EXTRACTION RULES — READ BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE

**Every single row in the register table MUST become one JSON record. No exceptions.**

This includes rows that many extractors incorrectly skip:

1. **"Same as" / "As Per" / "Similar To" reference rows** — These are SEPARATE, DISTINCT records. Extract each as its own record with `nata_sample_no` set to the literal reference string (e.g., "Same as 34511-039001").

2. **"Not Sampled" / "Assumed Positive" rows** — Items observed but not lab-tested are VALID entries. Extract them with `sample_result: "Assumed Positive"` or `sample_result: "Not Sampled"`.

3. **"No Access" rows** — Areas the assessor could not enter. Extract with `no_access: true`, `sample_result: null`.

**DO NOT skip, merge, or omit ANY table row.**

### PDF Text Formatting

Multi-word values are often split across multiple lines in PDF-extracted text:
- `Same as\n34511-039001` = one value: "Same as 34511-039001"
- `Assumed\npositive` = "Assumed Positive"
- `Non-friable` may appear as `Non friable`

## SF Vocabulary Mapping

Use these exact SF picklist values when mapping document text:

| Document Text | SF API Field | SF Picklist Value |
|---------------|-------------|-------------------|
| "Non Friable" / "Non-Friable" / "NF" | Friability_of_Material__c | Non-friable |
| "Friable" / "F" | Friability_of_Material__c | Friable |
| "Good Condition" / "Good" / "G" | Condition__c | Stable |
| "Fair" / "Fair Condition" | Condition__c | Fair |
| "Poor" / "Poor Condition" | Condition__c | Poor |
| "Low" (disturbance) | Disturbance_Potential_of_Material__c | Low |
| "Medium" / "Moderate" (disturbance) | Disturbance_Potential_of_Material__c | Moderate |
| "High" (disturbance) | Disturbance_Potential_of_Material__c | High |
| "Interior" / "Internal" / "Int" | Internal_External__c | Internal |
| "Exterior" / "External" / "Ext" | Internal_External__c | External |
| "Both" / "Internal & External" | Internal_External__c | External & Internal |
| "Positive" / "Pos" | Sample_Analysis_Result_Material_Status__c | Positive |
| "Assumed Positive" / "AP" / "Presumed Positive" | Sample_Analysis_Result_Material_Status__c | Assumed Positive |
| "Negative" / "Neg" | Sample_Analysis_Result_Material_Status__c | Negative |
| "Assumed Negative" / "AN" / "Presumed Negative" | Sample_Analysis_Result_Material_Status__c | Assumed Negative |
| "Neg - TAP" / "Treated as Positive" | Sample_Analysis_Result_Material_Status__c | Negative - Treated as Positive |

## SF Field Reference

Extract the following Salesforce Item__c fields per ACM register row:

| SF API Name | Label | Notes |
|-------------|-------|-------|
| `room_or_area` | Room or Area | Room name, area, or location identifier |
| `internal_external` | Internal/External | See picklist below |
| `level` | Level | Floor level (e.g., "Ground", "Level 1", "Roof") |
| `location_in_room` | Location in Room | Specific location (e.g., "Ceiling", "Wall", "Floor") |
| `friability_of_material` | Friability | See Friability_of_Material__c picklist |
| `acm_classification` | ACM Classification | See ACM_Classification__c picklist (product group) |
| `acm_sub_classification` | ACM Sub-Classification | Product type description |
| `item_name` | Item Name | See subsetted Item_Name__c list below |
| `if_other_item_name` | If Other Item Name | Free text — only when item_name = "Other" |
| `sample_result` | Sample Result | See Sample_Analysis_Result_Material_Status__c picklist |
| `nata_sample_no` | NATA Sample No | Sample number or reference string (e.g., "Same as 34511-039001") |
| `condition` | Condition | See Condition__c picklist |
| `disturbance_potential` | Disturbance Potential | See Disturbance_Potential_of_Material__c picklist |
| `quantity` | Quantity | Numeric value (float) — strip units |
| `labelled` | Labelled | "Yes" or "No" |
| `labelled_details` | Label Details | Free text label description if labelled |
| `hygienist_recommendations` | Hygienist Recommendations | Free text |
| `additional_comments` | Additional Comments | Free text |
| `no_access` | No Access | true if area was inaccessible |
| `data_issues` | Data Issues | List of data quality issues |
| `page_number` | Page Number | Page where this record appears |
| `extraction_confidence` | Confidence | "high" / "medium" / "low" |

