## Item_Name Usage Note

- Use one of the provided Item_Name options above — write the exact value including punctuation and capitalisation.
- Use `"Other"` if none of the provided options match, and fill `if_other_item_name` with the literal text from the document.
- Do NOT invent new Item_Name values outside the provided list.

## Output Format

Respond with a single JSON object matching the `ACMItemExtractionResult` schema:

```json
{
  "records": [
    {
      "room_or_area": ...,
      "internal_external": ...,
      "level": ...,
      "location_in_room": ...,
      "friability_of_material": ...,
      "acm_classification": ...,
      "acm_sub_classification": ...,
      "item_name": ...,
      "if_other_item_name": ...,
      "sample_result": ...,
      "nata_sample_no": ...,
      "condition": ...,
      "disturbance_potential": ...,
      "quantity": ...,
      "labelled": ...,
      "labelled_details": ...,
      "hygienist_recommendations": ...,
      "additional_comments": ...,
      "no_access": false,
      "extraction_confidence": "high" | "medium" | "low",
      "data_issues": [],
      "page_number": null
    }
  ],
  "status": "valid" | "no_acm_data" | "invalid",
  "extraction_notes": null
}
```

If there are no ACM items in this building section, return `{"records": [], "status": "no_acm_data", "extraction_notes": "..."}`.
